WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.920
I want to talk a little bit about&nbsp;
the repercussions and the fallout,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.960
including positive fallout from the&nbsp;
suspension of Donald Trump from Twitter.&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:16.800
Now we can have a reasonable debate about the&nbsp;
suspension of Donald Trump from Twitter. There's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.680
no question that he did violate the terms and&nbsp;
conditions of Twitter and he's been violating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.240
them for years. And if any non president were&nbsp;
doing that, they would have been suspended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.560
from Twitter long ago. At the same time, the&nbsp;
counterpoint would be that there's value in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.320
hearing from what world leaders say, and thus&nbsp;
the suspension is in some way a detriment to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.280
knowing what it is that our leaders are feeling&nbsp;
and saying and doing or whatever the case may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.440
be. I don't want to focus on that in this&nbsp;
particular segment because there have been a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.960
lot of headlines floating around that election.
Misinformation has dropped dramatically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.120
since Donald Trump was banned from Twitter. And&nbsp;
of course, that's true. It absolutely has. Online&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:05.680
misinformation about election fraud is down 73&nbsp;
percent after not only Twitter, but several social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:12.720
media sites suspended Donald Trump about eight,&nbsp;
nine, ten days ago. This is based on a report from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:19.280
Zainal Labs. And when you look at this, if you&nbsp;
believe that the sole cause of the reduction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:27.120
disinformation is Trump's suspension from these&nbsp;
platforms, that is a big endorsement of this as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:34.640
policy that if you identify particularly&nbsp;
important sort of nodes of disinformation by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:41.360
getting rid of them, you stop the trickle down,&nbsp;
as it effectively is of disinformation. Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:46.880
with what were, I think, 80 or something million&nbsp;
followers on Twitter would tweet disinformation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.400
And then these kind of next level people like his&nbsp;
family and prominent journalists and influencers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:58.560
would retweeting and signal boost the same bogus&nbsp;
ideas? And then you would have lower level media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.600
and voters. And it continues and continues. And&nbsp;
next thing you know, you know, your great aunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.000
who's not even on Twitter is hearing about some&nbsp;
of these ideas Sunday morning on Fox Business to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.080
point to Maria Bartiromo as as an example. I think&nbsp;
that the analysis has to go a little bit deeper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:22.000
though, because when Donald Trump was suspended&nbsp;
from Twitter and from these other platforms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.960
other things also went on that would explain&nbsp;
the dramatic reduction and disinformation around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:34.560
the election. And we can't say it was merely&nbsp;
suspending Trump. For example, about 70000 Cunanan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:41.040
associated accounts were purged from Twitter.
At the same time, it's not just Trump being gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.120
It's Twitter buckling down on a lot&nbsp;
of these signal boosting accounts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:53.440
sanctions on a parlor in so far as Apple and&nbsp;
Google said, no more parler on our app stores.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.080 --> 00:03:01.280
And Amazon said we're not hosting Parler&nbsp;
anymore. That's also a factor in reducing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:07.920
the spread of this election disinformation. The&nbsp;
election was also certified and the capital got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:14.400
stormed and it created a completely new look&nbsp;
at the circumstances for a lot of people.&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.320
So I just don't think we can point merely to&nbsp;
Trump being suspended and saying that's why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:26.400
election disinformation is down 73 percent. To say&nbsp;
it's down 73 percent because Trump was banned from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:32.160
Twitter seems like a stretch to me. To say&nbsp;
it coincided along with these other reasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.000
makes a lot of sense to me. And part of me hopes&nbsp;
that this will help to deprogram some people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:44.240
have fallen into fanaticism. But unfortunately,&nbsp;
if you believe that it wasn't disinformation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:50.160
in other words, if you hear me say election&nbsp;
disinformation is down 73 percent and your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:56.640
reaction is that wasn't disinformation. The truth&nbsp;
about the elections is down 73 percent because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.720
they're censoring it, then the fact that I'm&nbsp;
reporting this will become part of the conspiracy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:08.400
And as I've said before, it's very hard to&nbsp;
argue against folks who are committed to those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.800
narratives. I will say one other thing.&nbsp;
We've talked a lot about the importance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.280
of deprogramming, deprogramming, trumpet's and&nbsp;
deprogramming conspiracy theorists and the like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:23.440
on tomorrow's show, we are going or maybe on&nbsp;
Friday, but I'm hoping it'll be tomorrow if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:29.440
we have time for it. We are going to do a deep&nbsp;
dove on a recent focus group that was done with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:37.600
Trump voters. It's unbelievable. Frank Luntz did&nbsp;
a focus group with 12 Trump after the January 6th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:46.160
riots and everything about this focus group. Tells&nbsp;
us what we need to know about the uphill battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:53.040
of deprogramming trumpets and in particular the&nbsp;
role that right wing radical media has on it being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:57.200
so difficult to deprogram them. So tomorrow or&nbsp;
Friday, we're going to do a deep dove into that.

